Signet is a multi-factor authentication server written in Go.
It handles password, WebAuthn and email+PIN authentication.
It delivers a signed cookie to the
user's browser which dependent web applications can validate
via a synchronous REST API.

Signet stores user accounts in a CSV file and sessions,
WebAuthn credentials, and API client registrations in SQLite3.
It supports external claims hooks via subprocess communication
for integrating with directory services or policy engines.
